Collective variables for the 2D metadynamics FES of Ace-Cys-Nme
================================================================
NOTICE: SYNTHETIC SELF-TEST ARTIFACT. The OpenMM simulation was NOT executed in this sandbox (openmm not importable, no network). These files were generated by `python analysis.py --selftest` from a SYNTHETIC well-tempered-metadynamics deposition history to validate the numerical pipeline only. Run `python analysis.py` in an environment with openmm>=8.0 to obtain production results.

cv1 = phi (backbone), degrees, periodic 360, grid [-180, 180)
    dihedral( C of ACE(res1) - N(res2) - CA(res2) - C(res2) )
cv2 = psi (backbone), degrees, periodic 360, grid [-180, 180)
    dihedral( N(res2) - CA(res2) - C(res2) - N of NME(res3) )

Atom indices (0-based, order of ATOM records in data/dipeptide.pdb):
    phi: 4 (C, ACE) - 6 (N) - 8 (CA) - 15 (C)
    psi: 6 (N) - 8 (CA) - 15 (C) - 17 (N, NME)
Dihedral convention: standard IUPAC signed dihedral, angle = atan2(y, x) with
b1 normalized, v = b0-(b0.b1)b1, w = b2-(b2.b1)b1, x = v.w, y = (b1 x v).w;
computed identically from positions in this script and inside OpenMM via the
CustomCVForce Torsion collective variables.

Rationale: in vacuum the accessible conformational ensemble of a blocked
dipeptide is fully characterized by the two backbone dihedrals; side-chain
(chi1) rotamers are sterically locked by the ff14SB bonded terms at 300 K and
the peptide bond (omega) is fixed in the trans well (see below). Both dihedrals
are 360-periodic: the alpha (psi ~ -60 deg) and beta/collagen-like
(psi ~ +150 deg) basins would be indistinguishable on a [0,180) grid, hence
the full [-180, 180) range with 72x72 cell-centered bins (5 deg cells).

fes_2d.npy layout: fes[i, j], i -> phi cell (center -177.5 + 5*i deg),
j -> psi cell (same rule). Units kJ/mol; global minimum shifted to 0.0.

Metadynamics: well-tempered, T = 300.0 K, bias factor lambda = 15.0
(DeltaT = 4200 K), Gaussian height h0 = 1.0 kJ/mol, sigma = 3.0 deg
on both CVs, deposition every 0.5 ps, Langevin 1/ps, NoCutoff,
ff14SB (amber14-all.xml), vacuum. The initial structure in the PDB is an
idealized planar build with the peptide bond in the CIS (omega = 0) geometry;
for production the NME fragment was rotated about the C-N bond to trans
(omega = 180) and minimized; omega is left unbiased during the simulation.
The FES was reconstructed by this script from the recorded deposition history
as F(s) = -[lambda/(lambda-1)] V(s, t_end) with V = sum_k h_k G(s - s_k);
no built-in free-energy retrieval or internal bias arrays were used.

Self-test: 60000 synthetic deposits, max deviation from known toy FES 3.47 kJ/mol over visited cells.